medium.com/tinystories-4ce620e569a4\"},{\"title\":\"hyper.ai\",\"url\":\"https://hyper.ai/cn/datasets/33032\"},{\"title\":\"The Tiny Model Revolution with Ronen Eldan and Yuanzhi Li of Microsoft Research\",\"url\":\"https://cognitiverevolution.ai/the-tiny-model-revolution-with-ronen-eldan-and-yuanzhi-li-of-microsoft-research\"},{\"title\":\"Source code for oumi.datasets.pretraining.tiny_stories\",\"url\":\"https://oumi.ai/docs/en/latest/_modules/oumi/datasets/pretraining/tiny_stories.html\"},{\"title\":\"www.alphaxiv.org\",\"url\":\"https://www.alphaxiv.org/overview/2504.09184\"},{\"title\":\"🚀NEW COURSEVibe Coding AI Apps with Claude Code 🤖✨Enroll now\",\"url\":\"https://academy.dair.ai/papers/tinystories\"},{\"title\":\"Go backThe blogThis article\",\"url\":\"https://sfcompute.com/blog/tiny-narrations\"},{\"title\":\"meilu.jpshuntong.com\",\"url\":\"https://meilu.jpshuntong.com/url-68747470733a2f2f61727869762e6f7267/pdf/2305.07759.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"www.wizwand.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.wizwand.com/dataset/tinystories\"}]\n\nTinyStories is a synthetic dataset of short children's stories from Microsoft Research, introduced in a 2023 arXiv paper by Ronen Eldan and Yuanzhi Li.\n\n- **Content and purpose:** The stories were generated by GPT-3.5 and GPT-4 and use vocabulary suited to 3- to 4-year-olds. Researchers built it to train and evaluate small language models. (In this work, we introduce TinyStories, a synthetic dataset of short stories that only contain words that a typical 3 to 4-year-olds usually understand, generated by GPT-3.5 and GPT-4.)\n- **Versions and access:** It's hosted on Hugging Face as roneneldan/TinyStories. A newer TinyStoriesV2-GPT4-train.txt file uses only GPT-4 generations, since the original's GPT-3.5 stories are of lower quality. One source lists the license as CDLA-Sharing-1.0.\n- **Derivatives:** A Multilingual TinyStories corpus covers 17 Indian languages. Researchers at ETH Zürich and collaborators introduce SimpleStories, a parameterized synthetic text generation framework and dataset that improves upon TinyStories. SFCompute also released a synthetic audio dataset based on TinyStories.\n- **Criticism:** One analysis found that 59% of TinyStories samples began with the formulaic phrase \"Once upon a time,\" creating a highly repetitive dataset.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "26a62951-4ded-434d-8467-7de922b46664", "uuid": "2a7789d9-3dd4-4f63-b092-71ccf79348d5", "timestamp": "2026-11-02T08:59:12.215Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "TinyStories", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_014qS8qZ6tTdDKQnK8Njkt4S", "content": [{"title": "TinyStories: How Small Can Language Models Be and Still Speak Coherent English?", "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2305.07759"}, {"title": "hyper.ai", "url": "https://hyper.ai/en/datasets/33032"}, {"title": "www.huggingface.co", "url": "https://www.huggingface.co/datasets/roneneldan/TinyStories/blob/main/README.md?code=true"}, {"title": "huggingface.co", "url": "https://huggingface.co/datasets/roneneldan/TinyStories"}, {"title": "Multilingual TinyStories: A Synthetic Combinatorial Corpus of Indic Children's Stories for Training Small Language Models", "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2603.14563"}, {"title": "TinyStories: How Small Can Language Models Be and Still Speak Coherent English?", "url": "https://deepai.org/publication/tinystories-how-small-can-language-models-be-and-still-speak-coherent-english"}, {"title": "TinyStories: How Small Can Language Models Be and Still Speak Coherent English?", "url": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/?p=973236"}, {"title": "Loading Events", "url": "https://www.math.harvard.edu/event/the-tinystories-dataset-how-small-can-language-models-be-and-still-speak-coherent-english/"}, {"title": "Loading Events", "url": "https://cmsa.fas.harvard.edu/event/nt-92023"}, {"title": "TinyStories: How Small Can Language Models Be and Still Speak Coherent\\n English?", "url": "https://liner.com/ko/review/tinystories-how-small-can-language-models-be-and-still-speak"}, {"title": "tinystories small language models that still speak coherent", "url": "https://www.alignmentforum.[scrubbed:long-base64]"}, {"title": "Quick review", "url": "https://liner.com/review/tinystories-how-small-can-language-models-be-and-still-speak"}, {"title": "tinystories 4ce620e569a4", "url": "https://cobusgreyling.medium.com/tinystories-4ce620e569a4"}, {"title": "hyper.ai", "url": "https://hyper.ai/cn/datasets/33032"}, {"title": "The Tiny Model Revolution with Ronen Eldan and Yuanzhi Li of Microsoft Research", "url": "https://cognitiverevolution.ai/the-tiny-model-revolution-with-ronen-eldan-and-yuanzhi-li-of-microsoft-research"}, {"title": "Source code for oumi.datasets.pretraining.tiny_stories", "url": "https://oumi.ai/docs/en/latest/_modules/oumi/datasets/pretraining/tiny_stories.html"}, {"title": "www.alphaxiv.org", "url": "https://www.alphaxiv.org/overview/2504.09184"}, {"title": "🚀NEW COURSEVibe Coding AI Apps with Claude Code 🤖✨Enroll now", "url": "https://academy.dair.ai/papers/tinystories"}, {"title": "Go backThe blogThis article", "url": "https://sfcompute.com/blog/tiny-narrations"}, {"title": "meilu.jpshuntong.com", "url": "https://meilu.jpshuntong.com/url-68747470733a2f2f61727869762e6f7267/pdf/2305.07759.pdf"}, {"title": "www.wizwand.com", "url": "https://www.wizwand.com/dataset/tinystories"}]}, "TinyStories is a synthetic dataset of short children's stories from Microsoft Research, introduced in a 2023 arXiv paper by Ronen Eldan and Yuanzhi Li.\n\n- **Content and purpose:** The stories were generated by GPT-3.5 and GPT-4 and use vocabulary suited to 3- to 4-year-olds. Researchers built it to train and evaluate small language models. (In this work, we introduce TinyStories, a synthetic dataset of short stories that only contain words that a typical 3 to 4-year-olds usually understand, generated by GPT-3.